# TypeScript

## Strictness

- No `any`. No implicit `any`. Avoid `as unknown as T` unless isolated and justified.
- Prefer `unknown` + narrowing at boundaries.
- Export explicit types for public package APIs; infer locally when it stays readable.

## Imports

- Use package names (`@product/contract`) across boundaries.
- Avoid deep relative imports that escape a package root.

## Nullability

Be honest about `null` vs `undefined`. Match Prisma and contract schemas rather than normalizing ad hoc.

## Async

Surface errors; do not swallow. Nest filters / oRPC errors map to safe client payloads.
